Package: @PKG_NAME@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: pdchristian <cpopp@hotmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALL_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-pyqt6, python3-cryptography (>= 41.0),
 python3-psutil, python3-pamela, libpam0g, iputils-ping, iproute2, libqt6svg6
Recommends: freerdp2-x11, avahi-daemon
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/pdchristian/WOL-Ubuntu
Description: Wake-on-LAN manager with remote shutdown and live dashboards
 Modern "Control Center" desktop application for sending Wake-on-LAN magic
 packets to devices on the local network.
 .
 Features device management (card/list views), parallel wake-up, ping based
 status monitoring, network scanning, schedules with remote shutdown, an
 activity log with CSV export, remote desktop via FreeRDP and per-device
 dashboards showing live CPU/RAM/GPU/VRAM metrics, watched-process status
 chips (incl. llama.cpp model detection) plus remote script execution.
 .
 The package also installs the WOL Host Service ("wol-host-service"), a
 systemd service listening on TCP port 8765 that lets other Wake-on-LAN
 Manager clients (Windows, Ubuntu, Android) shut down or reboot this machine
 and read its metrics. Credential checks run through PAM; batch execution is
 disabled by default and must be enabled explicitly with
 "sudo wol-host-service --enable-batch". GPU/VRAM metrics additionally use
 nvidia-smi when an NVIDIA driver is present.
